      <data key="d1">"Peter Cratchit is the eldest son of Bob Cratchit, part of the Cratchit family in A Christmas Carol."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9e3921da66da5d761ab73cd849af6c43</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TIM CRATCHIT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Also known as Tiny Tim, Tim Cratchit is the youngest son of Bob Cratchit, characterized by his hopeful spirit despite his physical disability."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9e3921da66da5d761ab73cd849af6c43</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MR. FEZZIWIG&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Mr. Fezziwig is a jovial and kind-hearted old merchant known for his generosity and the employer of Ebenezer Scrooge in his youth."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9e3921da66da5d761ab73cd849af6c43</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FRED&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Fred is Ebenezer Scrooge's cheerful and persistent nephew who invites Scrooge to Christmas dinner every year."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fred is Scrooge's nephew, whom Scrooge asks to be let in for dinner, showing a familial connection."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9e3921da66da5d761ab73cd849af6c43&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-89777b838d5447c7bd1ec11282c4ee89</data>
      <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 2}]</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GHOST OF CHRISTMAS PAST&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Ghost of Christmas Past is a spirit that shows Scrooge scenes from his past to reflect on his life choices."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9e3921da66da5d761ab73cd849af6c43</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GHOST OF CHRISTMAS PRESENT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Ghost of Christmas Present is a spirit full of kindness and generosity, showing Scrooge the joy and hardship of others during Christmas."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9e3921da66da5d761ab73cd849af6c43</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GHOST OF CHRISTMAS YET TO COME&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Ghost of Christmas Yet to Come is a foreboding apparition that reveals the possible future consequences of Scrooge's actions."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9e3921da66da5d761ab73cd849af6c43</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GHOST OF JACOB MARLEY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Ghost of Jacob Marley is depicted as a specter who warns Scrooge about the consequences of a life focused solely on business and neglecting the welfare of others."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Ghost of Jacob Marley is the specter of Scrooge's deceased business partner, who warns him to change his ways."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9e3921da66da5d761ab73cd849af6c43&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-359187e7571bda4b0b08b2e0b6581e52</data>
      <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 1}]</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;JOE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Joe is a character involved in a conversation about bed-curtains, signifying his presence in the setting."&lt;SEP&gt;"Joe is a marine-store dealer who buys stolen goods, including items from Scrooge's home in a future vision."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9e3921da66da5d761ab73cd849af6c43&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-89777b838d5447c7bd1ec11282c4ee89</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;EBENEZER SCROOGE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Ebenezer Scrooge is a character depicted as a man of worldly mind, initially skeptical of the supernatural, and deeply linked to themes of reflection and regret."&lt;SEP&gt;"Ebenezer Scrooge is the main character, initially a miserly old man who learns to embrace the spirit of Christmas."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9e3921da66da5d761ab73cd849af6c43&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-359187e7571bda4b0b08b2e0b6581e52</data>
      <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 1}]</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MR. TOPPER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Mr. Topper is a bachelor and a character who appears at Fred's Christmas party."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9e3921da66da5d761ab73cd849af6c43</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DICK WILKINS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Dick Wilkins was a fellow apprentice with Scrooge during his youth, providing warmth to the memory of Scrooge's past."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9e3921da66da5d761ab73cd849af6c43</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BELLE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Belle is an old sweetheart of Scrooge, who left him due to his growing obsession with wealth."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9e3921da66da5d761ab73cd849af6c43</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CAROLINE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Caroline is the wife of one of Scrooge's debtors who feels joy at Scrooge's changed attitude."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9e3921da66da5d761ab73cd849af6c43</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MRS. CRATCHIT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Mrs. Cratchit is the wife of Bob Cratchit, known for her caring nature and devotion to her family."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9e3921da66da5d761ab73cd849af6c43</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BELINDA CRATCHIT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Belinda Cratchit is one of the daughters in the Cratchit family."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9e3921da66da5d761ab73cd849af6c43</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MARTHA CRATCHIT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Martha Cratchit is the eldest daughter of Bob and Mrs. Cratchit."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9e3921da66da5d761ab73cd849af6c43</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MRS. DILBER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Mrs. Dilber is a laundress who sells items stolen from Scrooge's house in one of the future visions."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9e3921da66da5d761ab73cd849af6c43</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FAN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Fan is Scrooge's sister, who appears in memories of the past to show their close relationship."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9e3921da66da5d761ab73cd849af6c43</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MRS. FEZZIWIG&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Mrs. Fezziwig is mentioned in the context of dancing with Old Fezziwig, indicating her presence at a celebration."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mrs. Fezziwig is the wife of Mr. Fezziwig, who enjoys the festive cheer of Christmas."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9e3921da66da5d761ab73cd849af6c43&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-89777b838d5447c7bd1ec11282c4ee89</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SCROOGE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Scrooge is a central character depicted as a miserly businessman with little fancy or imagination, living alone in a dreary suite of rooms once belonging to his deceased partner."&lt;SEP&gt;"Scrooge is a character known for his miserly and unsympathetic attitude, especially towards Christmas and charitable causes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Scrooge is a character who exhibits skepticism and fearlessness in the face of unusual occurrences in his home, haunted by thoughts of Marley."&lt;SEP&gt;"Scrooge is a character who is cynical and dismissive of Christmas, valuing financial wealth over social good and joy."&lt;SEP&gt;"Scrooge is a character who is skeptical and initially disbelieving of the supernatural events happening around him. He is confronted with the ghost of his former partner, Jacob Marley, and is forced to grapple with the reality of the apparition."&lt;SEP&gt;"Scrooge is a tight-fisted, covetous old sinner, known for his solitary nature and business acumen. He was the sole friend and business partner of Marley."&lt;SEP&gt;"Scrooge is described as a cold and miserly old man, solitary and indifferent to human sympathy, known for his grating voice and disdain for Christmas."&lt;SEP&gt;"Scrooge is the main character who is interacting with Jacob Marley's Ghost, expressing apprehension about the visit of the three spirits."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9c43dac2fcd5b578242d907ea6f8fc7b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-90d5764e301321c087f5a8f78b73a145&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1aa50206d02ed89418f65f97c6441d1c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d9aac3484185ac66045df92214d245d5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-74e2466de2f67fd710ef2f20c0a8d9e0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5dac41b3f9eeaf794f0147400b1718cd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-89777b838d5447c7bd1ec11282c4ee89&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-44d647b83223cc8b53863d27ac7cc4bf</data>
      <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 2}]</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MARLEY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Marley is Scrooge's deceased business partner, whose face appears supernaturally on the knocker of Scrooge's door."&lt;SEP&gt;"Marley is Scrooge's deceased business partner, whose memory haunts Scrooge and whose ghostly apparition appears before him."&lt;SEP&gt;"Marley was the deceased business partner of Scrooge and is pivotal to the story as his death sets the stage for the events that unfold."&lt;SEP&gt;"Marley, known as Marley's Ghost in this context, is the deceased former business partner of Scrooge. He appears as a ghostly figure, bound with chains made of cash-boxes, keys, padlocks, ledgers, deeds, and heavy purses. He has come to deliver an important message to Scrooge."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-89777b838d5447c7bd1ec11282c4ee89&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9c43dac2fcd5b578242d907ea6f8fc7b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1aa50206d02ed89418f65f97c6441d1c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d9aac3484185ac66045df92214d245d5</data>
      <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 2}]</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ST. PAUL'S CHURCHYARD&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"St. Paul's Churchyard is mentioned as a breezy spot in the story, used metaphorically to emphasize an unlikely event."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-89777b838d5447c7bd1ec11282c4ee89</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SCROOGE AND MARLEY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Scrooge and Marley is the name of the firm co-owned by Scrooge and Marley, known for its business transactions."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-89777b838d5447c7bd1ec11282c4ee89</data>
      <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 2}]</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TIM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Tim is a character described as being carried back from church, indicating his involvement in a situation with family dynamics."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-89777b838d5447c7bd1ec11282c4ee89</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FEZZIWIG&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Old Fezziwig is a character who is depicted participating in a dance, portraying a scene of festivity."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-89777b838d5447c7bd1ec11282c4ee89</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MARLEY'S GHOST&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Marley's Ghost is the supernatural event marking the return of Marley as a ghost, significant to the narrative's plot."&lt;SEP&gt;"Marley's Ghost marks the supernatural event where Marley appears to Scrooge as a ghost to convey an essential message, challenging Scrooge's disbelief."&lt;SEP&gt;"Marley's Ghost refers to the spectral appearance of Scrooge's deceased business partner, signifying unresolved issues from the past."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-89777b838d5447c7bd1ec11282c4ee89&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9c43dac2fcd5b578242d907ea6f8fc7b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1aa50206d02ed89418f65f97c6441d1c</data>
      <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 3}]</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SCROOGE'S NEPHEW&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Scrooge's Nephew is a cheerful and lively character who tries to engage Scrooge in the festive spirit of Christmas."&lt;SEP&gt;"Scrooge's nephew is a character who values Christmas as a time for kindness and tries to build a relationship with his uncle despite resistance."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-74e2466de2f67fd710ef2f20c0a8d9e0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5dac41b3f9eeaf794f0147400b1718cd</data>
