      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;SCROOGE&quot;" target="&quot;CHRISTMAS EVE&quot;">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Scrooge experiences a confrontation with his Nephew on Christmas Eve, highlighting Scrooge's negative view of the holiday season."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-74e2466de2f67fd710ef2f20c0a8d9e0</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;SCROOGE&quot;" target="&quot;CLERK&quot;">
      <data key="d4">6.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"The clerk works under Scrooge, showing warmth despite Scrooge's cold demeanor and minimal salary policy."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-5dac41b3f9eeaf794f0147400b1718cd</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;SCROOGE&quot;" target="&quot;MR. MARLEY&quot;">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Scrooge and Mr. Marley were business partners who shared a similar business mentality and values."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-5dac41b3f9eeaf794f0147400b1718cd</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;SCROOGE&quot;" target="&quot;THE PORTLY GENTLEMEN&quot;">
      <data key="d4">5.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"The gentlemen interact with Scrooge to solicit charitable contributions, meeting resistance to their cause."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-5dac41b3f9eeaf794f0147400b1718cd</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;SCROOGE&quot;" target="&quot;SCROOGE AND MARLEY'S&quot;">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Scrooge is the surviving partner and current representative of the business firm Scrooge and Marley's."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-5dac41b3f9eeaf794f0147400b1718cd</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;SCROOGE&quot;" target="&quot;UNION WORKHOUSES&quot;">
      <data key="d4">7.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Scrooge mentions the Union Workhouses as establishments that he supports financially, suggesting they are sufficient for helping the poor."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-90d5764e301321c087f5a8f78b73a145</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;SCROOGE&quot;" target="&quot;POOR LAW&quot;">
      <data key="d4">7.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Scrooge refers to the Poor Law as part of the system he supports instead of giving charity, showing his belief in its effectiveness."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-90d5764e301321c087f5a8f78b73a145</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;SCROOGE&quot;" target="&quot;CHRISTMAS&quot;">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Scrooge's dismissive attitude toward Christmas highlights his lack of festive spirit and generosity."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-90d5764e301321c087f5a8f78b73a145</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;SCROOGE&quot;" target="&quot;COUNTING-HOUSE&quot;">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Scrooge spends significant time in the Counting-House, reflecting his focus on work over social and familial connections."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-90d5764e301321c087f5a8f78b73a145</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;SCROOGE&quot;" target="&quot;SCROOGE'S HOUSE&quot;">
      <data key="d4">10.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Scrooge's presence and actions are primarily situated in his house, where the eerie events and sightings occur."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-9c43dac2fcd5b578242d907ea6f8fc7b</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;SCROOGE&quot;" target="&quot;JACOB MARLEY'S GHOST&quot;">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Scrooge is visited by Jacob Marley's Ghost, who warns him about his possible fate and the impending visits from the Three Spirits."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-44d647b83223cc8b53863d27ac7cc4bf</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;SCROOGE&quot;" target="&quot;THREE SPIRITS&quot;">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Scrooge is informed by Jacob Marley's Ghost that he will be visited by the Three Spirits, which is integral to the narrative of his redemption."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-44d647b83223cc8b53863d27ac7cc4bf</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;MARLEY'S GHOST&quot;" target="&quot;SCROOGE'S HOUSE&quot;">
      <data key="d4">7.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Marley's Ghost manifests within Scrooge's House, causing strange phenomena inside the house."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-9c43dac2fcd5b578242d907ea6f8fc7b</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;MARLEY'S GHOST&quot;" target="&quot;THE GHOST&quot;">
      <data key="d4">10.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Marley's Ghost and The Ghost are the same entity, representing Marley in his spectral form, conveying the significance of his message to Scrooge."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-1aa50206d02ed89418f65f97c6441d1c</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;THE GENTLEMAN&quot;" target="&quot;UNION WORKHOUSES&quot;">
      <data key="d4">6.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"The Gentleman discusses the limitations of Union Workhouses as part of his argument for collecting donations."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-90d5764e301321c087f5a8f78b73a145</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;THE GENTLEMAN&quot;" target="&quot;POOR LAW&quot;">
      <data key="d4">6.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"The Gentleman implies that the Poor Law, while busy, does not adequately address the needs of the poor, motivating his appeal for charity."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-90d5764e301321c087f5a8f78b73a145</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;THE LORD MAYOR&quot;" target="&quot;MANSION HOUSE&quot;">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"The Lord Mayor organizes a grand Christmas celebration at the Mansion House, reflecting his position and responsibilities."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-90d5764e301321c087f5a8f78b73a145</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;THE LORD MAYOR&quot;" target="&quot;LITTLE TAILOR&quot;">
      <data key="d4">6.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"The Lord Mayor's emphasis on Christmas contrasts with the Little Tailor's humble circumstances, yet both are part of the festive city's tapestry."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-90d5764e301321c087f5a8f78b73a145</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;FOG&quot;" target="&quot;LINKS&quot;">
      <data key="d4">7.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"The Links guide people through the Fog, emphasizing the challenges of navigation and the reliance on offered services during this period."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-90d5764e301321c087f5a8f78b73a145</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;LABOURERS&quot;" target="&quot;RAGGED MEN AND BOYS&quot;">
      <data key="d4">6.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Labourers and Ragged Men and Boys both represent societal reactions to the cold and highlight class differences during the festive season."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-90d5764e301321c087f5a8f78b73a145</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;RAGGED MEN AND BOYS&quot;" target="&quot;POULTERERS AND GROCERS&quot;">
      <data key="d4">5.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"The bustling trades of Poulterers and Grocers contrast with the plight of the Ragged Men and Boys, underscoring social disparities."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-90d5764e301321c087f5a8f78b73a145</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;JACOB MARLEY&quot;" target="&quot;MARLEY'S CHAIN&quot;">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Jacob Marley's misdeeds and lifestyle have resulted in the burden of Marley's Chain, which he carries as a ghost and serves as a poignant warning to Scrooge."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-1aa50206d02ed89418f65f97c6441d1c</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
  </graph>
</graphml>
